WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — satiation (90s) AI-synthesized studio narration

1
00:00:02.288 --> 00:00:07.499
Sorting a sorted array twice or re-proving a checked theorem produces zero marginal value:

2
00:00:07.499 --> 00:00:08.715
the task is satiated.

3
00:00:14.759 --> 00:00:20.461
Formalizing intensive per-task satiation alongside extensive task-entry elasticity shows

4
00:00:20.461 --> 00:00:24.283
how falling per-task joules coexist with rising total load.

5
00:00:30.327 --> 00:00:34.864
This three-dimensional surface contrasts the flat post-completion plateau of a

6
00:00:34.864 --> 00:00:38.936
single task against expanding task horizons and physical power floors.

7
00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:52.917
Per-token billing rewards verbose retries past satiation, whereas completion-gated systems halt the moment verification succeeds.

8
00:00:58.961 --> 00:01:05.084
Empirical inference pricing curves fall orders of magnitude faster than silicon joules per operation,

9
00:01:05.084 --> 00:01:06.781
exposing the physical floor.

10
00:01:12.825 --> 00:01:17.321
Interactive satiation curves let readers test elasticity regimes directly;

11
00:01:17.321 --> 00:01:20.844
all energy terms are analytical rather than board-shunted.
